/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/docs/archive/tasking-2026-06-16.md:61:**Wrong:** `_browser_verified` (`engine.py:1764-1800`) passes if any :8000 browser observation has zero console errors — never inspects pixels; a blank-white/empty-body page passes (`:1581` admits the gap). Daemon already captures screenshots (`_browser_daemon.py:151-156`), unused by the gate. **Fix:** (1) cheap always-on: require a non-trivial paint signal (visible text length / non-blank screenshot bytes) — reject "console-clean but empty"; (2) vision arm when `DRIVER_VISION==1`: thread the screenshot into a fresh-context vision check (DoD-evaluator pattern), advisory-first, behind the existing `_finish_verify_refusals` cap (no livelock). **Acceptance:** blank :8000 page (clean console) is REFUSED; good page finishes first try; valve still releases after capped refusals. **Benefit:** closes the most common web "looks done, isn't" hole (blank screen / unmounted root). **Risk:** med — gate flakiness → finish livelock; mitigate via the existing cap + heuristic-blocking/vision-advisory.
