     1	"""`verify_web_app` — the build agent's self-test tool (W-45 v1).
     2	
     3	The build agent used to "verify" a web build by opening the page in the headless
     4	browser and eyeballing the console — but a raw page observation is EVIDENCE, not
     5	a VERDICT, so the agent re-loaded the same page 25-40 times without ever
     6	concluding. This tool closes that gap: given the running preview it runs the
     7	DETERMINISTIC user-centered checks (server reachable + HTTP 2xx/3xx + no console
     8	errors + no critical network failures + meaningful render) and returns a single
     9	structured PASS/FAIL/DEGRADED verdict the finish gate can consume directly.
    10	
    11	Reuse (no reinvention):
    12	  * `BrowserTool` (browser.py) — drives the headless navigate + console/network/
    13	    screenshot capture through the same sandbox browser daemon the agent uses.
    14	  * `port_owners` / preview-port detection (sandbox/port_owner.py, server.py) —
    15	    finds the live preview without the agent having to name a URL.
    16	  * `_browser_content_meaningful` (core/loop/finish.py) — the SAME blank-render
    17	    guard the finish gate already trusts, so "served 200 but mounted nothing"
    18	    reads identically here.
    19	
    20	The `failure_fingerprint` (a stable hash of the top console-error signatures +
    21	critical network failures) is THE loop-breaker key: the finish gate caches a
    22	verdict by it, so re-verifying WITHOUT a productive edit returns the same
    23	fingerprint and the gate can mark the run STUCK instead of reloading forever.
    24	"""
