REVISE

**Reasons**
- Audit verdict is mostly correct. Preview tools are host-owned and have no port arg; `serve` already emits `DeliverableEvent`; UI/harness consume `app|files`; HARN-2 has `ShowToUserOracle`. No rebuild is needed.
- `ArtifactContract.delivery_mode` as a derived `app|files` property is campaign-coherent, not scope invention. It matches the existing event/UI shape.
- Mapping is right: `appkit.leadgen`, `static.site`, `interactive.prototype` → `app`; `deck`, `document`, `workflow.output`, `custom` → `files`. `custom→files` is the safer default.
- Deferring the `handle_serve` reject wire is acceptable only if P5 is explicitly described as “contract shape + validator/accessor,” not runtime enforcement. The current plan overclaims “validator enforces shape” before it is wired.
- There is one P5-relevant substrate issue the plan should include: model-facing `serve`/`finish` schemas still mention fixed port `8000`, which conflicts with the host-owned preview rule.
- Also track synthetic app deliverables: `lifecycle._maybe_synthesize_app_deliverable` currently emits `artifact_kind="app"` for any snapshot with `index.html`, independent of the active contract. That can violate `custom→files`/deck/document expectations unless covered by the same follow-up enforcement.

**Required Revisions**
- Add a small P5 task or explicit follow-up to scrub fixed-port `8000` guidance from `serve` and `finish` tool descriptions.
- Reword “validator enforces shape” to “validator makes shape enforceable; runtime enforcement follows in handle_serve wire.”
- Expand the reject-wire follow-up to cover both `handle_serve` and synthetic lifecycle app deliverables.
